# Complete deterministic conversion of original models to binary FBX 7.7

Complete deterministic conversion of original models to binary FBX 7.7.

## Acceptance criteria

- [x] Complete deterministic conversion of original models to binary FBX 7.7.

## Dependencies

No explicit task dependency was recorded in the legacy TODO.

## Evidence

All four typed children are completed: model/world geometry is required before
reserving FBX-backed meshes, authored normals emit explicit smoothing metadata,
external PNG provenance is versioned without promoting sidecars, and the
package-level FBX catalog must be complete before import plans become ready.

Fresh stable-Rust validation ran the complete `fbx` package test suite. The
binary-only contract accepts only FBX 7700, deterministic model/character and
structural-guide writers remain green, and generated package-index tests retain
canonical package evidence. Pipeline validation additionally passed 23 Unreal
import-manifest tests and 12 generated FBX-catalog tests, including rejection of
partial/unclaimed catalogs, stale size/digest/version data, noncanonical fields,
and texture provenance drift. The explicit stale-version regression mutates an
artifact to FBX 7400 and requires rejection.
